# Copy to android/key.properties and fill in. That file is gitignored, as are
# *.jks and *.keystore — the upload key must never enter this repository.
#
# Only needed for a LOCAL release build. Codemagic supplies the same four values
# as CM_KEYSTORE_PATH / CM_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD / CM_KEY_ALIAS / CM_KEY_PASSWORD
# from the keystore uploaded to it, and app/build.gradle.kts prefers those.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ONE UPLOAD KEY FOR EVERY MGKFITNESS APP — Run, Lift, and whatever comes
# after. It already exists (created 2026-09-10); do not make a second one.
#
#   keytool -genkey -v -keystore mgkfitness-upload.jks \
#     -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000 -alias upload
#
# A Play listing records the upload certificate it expects. Nothing requires
# that certificate to be unique to one listing, so the same key serves all of
# them, and the benefit is the obvious one: a single secret to hold, back up
# and not lose.
#
# This file argued the opposite for a few hours — "one keystore per Play
# listing... a shared key means a compromise or a reset on one listing reaches
# the other for no benefit at all". The last clause was false, and the rest
# was a blast-radius argument with no scenario behind it. Both failure modes
# are recoverable identically anyway: Google resets a lost OR compromised
# upload key by support request.
#
# frunt is the permanent exception — live on Play under its own key, and a
# shipped listing's upload key cannot be swapped without that same support
# request for nothing in return.
#
# Play uses Google Play App Signing: this key signs the UPLOAD, and Google holds
# the key that signs what users install. Treat it as precious rather than
# irreplaceable.
#
# `storeFile` is an absolute path, or one relative to android/app/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

storeFile=/absolute/path/to/mgkfitness-upload.jks
storePassword=
keyAlias=upload
keyPassword=
